  {
    "element_type": "paragraph",
    "text": "Casual leave\nSick Leave",
    "page": 3,
    "heading_level": null,
    "heading_path": [
      "TECSACK India Policy - Leave Policy"
    ],
    "metadata": {
      "extraction_method": "pymupdf"
    }
  },
  {
    "element_type": "paragraph",
    "text": "The Employee is entitled to 12 Calendar days of paid Casual Leave every year.\nThe year for the purpose of Leave accounting is the financial year i.e. from April to\nMarch\nCasual leave is credited on every quarter of the year.\nUnutilised Casual leave will not carried forward to the next financial year.\nCasual leave should be applied in the system before five days of working day and\ninformed through mail to Supervisor and HR team.\nEmployee cannot apply continuous three casual leave.\nEmployee cannot apply more than two casual leaves in the month.\nOnce the Supervisor approval, the leave will be considered as paid leave, or else will\nconsidered as LOP.",
    "page": 3,
    "heading_level": null,
    "heading_path": [
      "TECSACK India Policy - Leave Policy"
    ],
    "metadata": {
      "extraction_method": "pymupdf"
    }
  },
  {
    "element_type": "paragraph",
    "text": "Types of Leave",
    "page": 3,
    "heading_level": null,
    "heading_path": [
      "TECSACK India Policy - Leave Policy"
    ],
    "metadata": {
      "extraction_method": "pymupdf"
    }
  },
  {
    "element_type": "paragraph",
    "text": "1.\n2.",
    "page": 3,
    "heading_level": null,
    "heading_path": [
      "TECSACK India Policy - Leave Policy"
    ],
    "metadata": {
      "extraction_method": "pymupdf"
    }
  },
  {
    "element_type": "paragraph",
    "text": "Eligibilty\nThis policy is applicable to all employees of Tecsack Software, India including\nTrainees and Full time Employees.",
    "page": 3,
    "heading_level": null,
    "heading_path": [
      "TECSACK India Policy - Leave Policy"
    ],
    "metadata": {
      "extraction_method": "pymupdf"
    }
  },
