  {
    "element_type": "paragraph",
    "text": "Employees serving Notice Period cannot avail Casual Leave if they have sufficient\nbalance.",
    "page": 4,
    "heading_level": null,
    "heading_path": [
      "TECSACK India Policy - Leave Policy"
    ],
    "metadata": {
      "extraction_method": "pymupdf"
    }
  },
  {
    "element_type": "paragraph",
    "text": "The Employee is entitled to 12 Calendar days of paid Sick Leave every year.\nThe year for the purpose of Leave accounting is the financial year i.e. from April to\nMarch\nSick leave is credited on a pro rata basis for trainees and probationers on\ncompletion of the first calendar quarter after the date of joining and thereafter, at\nthe end of each subsequent quarter.\nUnutilised leave may carried forward to the next financial year and the employee\nmay accumulate upto a maximum of 60 leave days. Number of days in excess of 60,\naccumulated up to that date are treated as “surplus” and will lapse without any\nencashment.\nSick leave must be availed only for an employee’s own medical reasons.\nLeave may be applied after availing the same, however it must be applied within 3\nworking days of reporting back from leave. If not applied within this period, the\nsupervisor may use his/her discretion to convert this into Loss of Pay.\nIf the employee applies for Sick Leave, but doesnot avail of the same due to any\nreason, he/she may choose to cancel the same.\nIncase the leave duration is >= 3 days, a Medical Certificate should be submitted to\nthe Supervisor.",
    "page": 4,
    "heading_level": null,
    "heading_path": [
      "TECSACK India Policy - Leave Policy"
    ],
    "metadata": {
      "extraction_method": "pymupdf"
    }
  },
  {
    "element_type": "paragraph",
    "text": "Employee serving Notice Period",
    "page": 4,
    "heading_level": null,
    "heading_path": [
      "TECSACK India Policy - Leave Policy"
    ],
    "metadata": {
      "extraction_method": "pymupdf"
    }
  },
  {
    "element_type": "paragraph",
    "text": "Sick Leave\nThe purpose of the Sick Leave Policy is to grant days off from work to an employee\nin the event of his/her illness or injury for medical treatment and /or recuperation.",
    "page": 4,
    "heading_level": null,
    "heading_path": [
      "TECSACK India Policy - Leave Policy"
    ],
    "metadata": {
      "extraction_method": "pymupdf"
    }
  },
